# Configuration, secrets, and the audit trail (docs/guide/how-config-and-audit.md).
title: Every write is logged in a hash chain, and audit checks that log against GitHub's own history
direction: down
config: Layered config names secrets, never values
secrets: Secrets: keychain, AAYU_SECRET_ env, age file
verb: A verb makes an external write
log: Actions log segments on the ledger
github: GitHub's event history
audit: aayu audit reconciles both into a report
config -> verb: settings
secrets -> verb: tokens and keys
verb -> log: redacted record
verb -> github: the write lands
log -> audit: what aayu did
github -> audit: source of record
